## 3. Database schema — the minimum viable version of the research report's schema

The research report's schema is correct; trim it to only what the prototype's three screens (visit list → sync calendars → ranked assignment) actually touch. Everything else (Communication_Logs escalation state machine, van/vehicle optimization, out-of-hours tally, skill-scarcity index) is **real and important, but deferred to §7 P1/P2** — build the skeleton columns now so migration later is additive, not a rewrite.

```python
# models.py — SQLAlchemy, one file

class Staff(Base):
    __tablename__ = "staff"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)
    name = Column(String, nullable=False)
    role = Column(String)                     # Clinician | Tech | GradStudent
    van_trained = Column(Boolean, default=False)
    in_lab_day = Column(Integer, nullable=True)   # 0=Mon ... 4=Fri, forbidden day for off-site
    out_of_hours_count = Column(Integer, default=0)   # deferred use, keep the column now

class Assessment(Base):
    __tablename__ = "assessment"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)
    name = Column(String, nullable=False)     # ADOS, Mullen, CSBS, Bayley, ...

class StaffAssessment(Base):
    __tablename__ = "staff_assessment"
    staff_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("staff.id"), primary_key=True)
    assessment_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("assessment.id"), primary_key=True)
    status = Column(String)                   # RELIABLE | IN_TRAINING

class Participant(Base):
    __tablename__ = "participant"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)
    study = Column(String)                    # NANO | IPSA | Sibling
    dob = Column(Date)
    due_date = Column(Date, nullable=True)    # for PT adjustment
    preferred_contact_method = Column(String) # Text | Email | Call  <-- the open item from the meeting
    van_inaccessible = Column(Boolean, default=False)

class Visit(Base):
    __tablename__ = "visit"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)
    participant_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("participant.id"))
    visit_month = Column(Integer)             # 1,2,3,6,9,12,24,36
    ideal_date = Column(Date)
    status = Column(String)                   # FUTURE | IN_PROGRESS | SCHEDULED | COMPLETED | RESCHEDULED | SKIPPED
    assigned_staff_ids = Column(String, nullable=True)  # simple CSV of staff.id for the prototype

class CalendarSyncRun(Base):
    __tablename__ = "calendar_sync_run"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)
    started_at = Column(DateTime)
    completed_at = Column(DateTime, nullable=True)

class CalendarBlock(Base):
    __tablename__ = "calendar_block"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)
    sync_run_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("calendar_sync_run.id"))
    staff_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("staff.id"))
    day = Column(Date)
    start_time = Column(Time)
    end_time = Column(Time)
    status = Column(String)                   # busy | free | unknown
    confidence = Column(Float)
    reviewed = Column(Boolean, default=False)  # did a human confirm this block?
    source_image_hash = Column(String, nullable=True)
```

Two deliberate simplifications vs. the fuller schema in the research doc, both reversible later:

- `assigned_staff_ids` as a CSV string instead of a join table — fine at this volume (a handful of coordinators, dozens of visits/month), and trivially normalized into a real join table once you actually need to query "all visits assigned to Sanjana" efficiently.
- No separate `Communication_Logs` table yet — `preferred_contact_method` lives directly on `Participant` for now, matching the meeting's ask to "confirm current family communication method," without standing up the full escalation state machine from the research report until §7 P1.

