## 5. Frontend additions — two screens, layered onto the existing Netlify site

### 5.1 "Sync Calendars" panel (extends `index.html`)

- One button, "Sync Calendars," plus a small per-coordinator upload slot (file picker, one per roster member) for the prototype's manual-capture stage. This matches the build order from the earlier discussion: manual upload first, automated print-trigger later.
- On click: `POST` all six images to `/api/sync-calendars`, show a simple per-coordinator checklist (✅/⚠️) as each result resolves, then auto-navigate to the review screen.
- A small "last synced: 2 minutes ago" label sourced from `CalendarSyncRun.completed_at`, always visible near the ranked-assignment view — this directly answers the meeting's "who knows the last time it pulled the calendars" concern without adding any new backend logic.

### 5.2 `sync-review.html` — the block-confirmation screen

- Fetch `GET /api/sync-runs/{run_id}/review`.
- For each coordinator, show their uploaded image with translucent colored rectangles drawn over the detected blocks (simple `<canvas>` overlay using the stored bounding-box coordinates), labeled with inferred time range and "busy."
- A checkmark/✗ per block; unconfirmed blocks stay `reviewed = False` and are excluded from `has_evidence_conflict` until confirmed — mirrors the "review before it counts" rule that was central to the earlier calendar-ingestion strategy.
- This is the single screen worth spending the most design time on: it's the artifact that lets you show the lab "yes, this is reading your calendar correctly" before anyone trusts it for real scheduling.

### 5.3 Ranked-assignment view (extends the existing dashboard)

- For a selected visit, call a new `GET /api/visits/{id}/ranked-candidates`, which wraps `rank_candidates`.
- Render as a simple ranked list/table: coordinator name, score, one-line reason, and — critically — a visibly distinct row style for `"insufficient calendar evidence — sync first"` results, so a scheduler is never left guessing why someone isn't ranked.
- Add the `preferred_contact_method` field from `Participant` right next to the visit header, satisfying the meeting's ask to "confirm current family communication method" as a visible, not buried, piece of context.

