## 6. What's intentionally NOT in this prototype (and why that's the right call)

| Deferred | Why it's safe to defer | Where it's already specced for later |
|---|---|---|
| Microsoft Graph `getSchedule` integration | Real API integration needs IT governance sign-off (Data Sharing Agreement, MFA, TLS 1.3) per the deep research report — a multi-week institutional process, not a coding task. The vision pipeline's evidence shape should stay swappable so Graph can replace it per-coordinator later. | Research report's "Enterprise Integration Alternative" section |
| Full Communication_Logs escalation state machine | The prototype only needs the *current* preferred channel surfaced, not the full multi-day escalation cron job, to satisfy this round's feedback. | Research report's "State Machine Implementation for Communication Protocols" |
| Van/vehicle optimization, skill-scarcity indexing, out-of-hours equity scoring | Real and valuable, but each is an independent scoring term that can be added to `scoring.py` incrementally without touching the sync pipeline or the DB shape defined here. | Research report's "Soft Constraint Optimization" section |
| Month-view PDF ingestion / multi-tier evidence doctrine (Tier 1/2/2.5/3) | That doctrine matters once multiple *kinds* of calendar evidence coexist (live API + PDF + vision capture). At prototype scale you have exactly one evidence source (vision capture), so the three-state `has_evidence_conflict` return already captures the one rule that matters ("don't guess") without needing the full tiering machinery. | Prior calendar-ingestion strategy doc |
| Background cron jobs (daily "Appointments to Schedule" shifting, nightly reconciliation) | Not needed until the visit list itself needs to auto-populate from participant DOB math; for the prototype, seed `Visit` rows manually or with a simple one-off script. | Research report's "Temporal Mathematics of Visit Windows" section |
| CI/CD, containerization, multi-environment config | Adds maintenance surface with no payoff until more than one person needs to deploy this. | — |

