## 7. Build order (this is the actual prompt sequence to execute, in order)

1. **`db.py` + `models.py`** — stand up SQLite, run `Base.metadata.create_all()`, write `seed_data.py` to load the current staff roster and reliability matrix from the scheduling manual (Emma, Sanjana, Lauren, Makenzie, Ramiro) plus a handful of test `Participant`/`Visit` rows.
2. **`vision.py`** — implement `extract_blocks` exactly as in §4.3, test it against 2–3 real single-coordinator calendar screenshots (day or work-week view — reject month-grid captures with a clear error message rather than silently mis-extracting them).
3. **`POST /api/sync-calendars`** in `app.py` — wire the upload loop to `vision.py`, write `CalendarSyncRun`/`CalendarBlock` rows.
4. **`sync-review.html`** — build the overlay-and-confirm screen; this is the artifact to demo back to the lab before building anything downstream of it.
5. **`constraints.py` + `scoring.py`** — implement `eligible_staff`, the three-state `has_evidence_conflict`, and the trimmed `score_pair`/`rank_candidates`.
6. **`GET /api/visits/{id}/ranked-candidates`** + the ranked-assignment view in the existing dashboard, including the visible "insufficient evidence" state and the `preferred_contact_method` field.
7. **Only after all six steps work end-to-end**, revisit §6's deferred list and pick the next single item to build — not all of them at once.

Each step produces something independently demoable, which is the actual point of keeping this unified and small: at every step of the build, you have a working system, not a half-finished multi-module architecture.
